              "text": "Before the new one: say tea, water and yoghurt. (चाय, पाणी, दही.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दूध",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूध — dūdh — \"milk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हूं रोज दूध पीऊं हूं। hū̃ roj dūdh pīū̃ hū̃. — I drink milk every day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It ends on a letter you have not written yet: dh, a द with a breath after it. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूध (dūdh) is inherited from Sanskrit dugdha, \"milk\", a word built on the verb for milking. CDIAL lists Marwari dūdh, masculine (CDIAL 6391)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दूध is masculine: दूध गरम है। (dūdh garam hai.), the milk is hot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
