    {
      "id": "MW-W46-dha",
      "sequence": 9650,
      "title": "ध (dha) — the letter that ends दूध (dūdh)",
      "headword": "ध",
      "romanization": "dha",
      "gloss": "dha — the letter that ends दूध",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-type",
        "writing-block",
        "script-block",
        "eyes-or-hands-step"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:00e328b5838bcf7e",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [
          "a pen and something to write on",
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page",
          "your eyes or your hands for the steps that ask you to read, point, write or gesture"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Warm-up",
          "Script you'll notice: ध",
          "Guided Practice",
          "Wrap-up Recall"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You will want a pen and something to write on, your eyes, for letter shapes on the page and your eyes or your hands for the steps that ask you to read, point, write or gesture. You can listen to everything else now. I will say so again when we reach them, but leave these sections until you have stopped: Warm-up, Script you'll notice: ध, Guided Practice and Wrap-up Recall."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: write द once, and name it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now say दूध (dūdh), \"milk\". It opens on द and ends on a द with a breath after it: dh. This lesson puts that letter in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: ध",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ध — dha, the breathed d."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It ends दूध (dūdh). It sits beside द as घ sits beside ग: the same place in the mouth, with a breath. On the page it is an upper spiral that ends in a shoulder, a lower bowl, and a right stem under the headline."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ध",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "1. start at the upper spiral's inner crossing, curl around the small opening, widen left and down around the outer loop, then sweep right through the shoulder."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "2. without lifting, turn back left along the shoulder to the left waist."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "3. sweep down and around the lower bowl to its right junction."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "4. climb up the right stem to the headline."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "5. descend the right stem top-to-bottom."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "6. lift and draw the top shirorekhā left-to-right."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pen lifts: 1."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The source shows four movements; native writers draw ध (dha) as two pen-down strokes (81% of HP Labs India's native-writer samples, 64 of 79). This ductus follows the four movements in order and direction, lifting only before the headline: after the shoulder the pen turns back along it into the lower bowl, then climbs the right stem before descending it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Stroke order is one attested teaching order; hands and teachers vary. Source: Opiaterein, ‘Deva-ध (dha)-order.gif’, strokes 1–4, Wikimedia Commons, 10 May 2009."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at दूध (dūdh) and point at ध (dha) at its end",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at **दूध** and point at ध at its end]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "TRACE",
              "instruction": "ध (dha) three times, saying dh as you finish each one",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU TRACE: ध three times, saying *dh* as you finish each one]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "द, then ध (dha), from memory",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: द, then ध, from memory]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "READ",
              "instruction": "दूध (dūdh) aloud once more",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU READ: **दूध** aloud once more]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which letter is this — ध? (dha, the breathed d.) Which word did it come from? (दूध, dūdh, \"milk\".)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "spoken": false,
              "id": "MW-W46-dha-recall",
              "prompt": "Write the letter that ends dūdh (milk).",
              "assesses": [
                "MW-SCRIPT-C155-DHA-01"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "ध"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "Yes: ध, from dūdh.",
                "incorrect": "The letter is ध. Find it at the end of दूध and write it once more."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
